    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie\n\nSherry FitzGerald Conor McManus are delighted to present Lynford, Latlurcan, Co. Monaghan to the market.\n\nA substantial detached residence occupying a generous site in an exceptionally convenient location on the outskirts of Monaghan town.\n\nThe property offers spacious accommodation over two floors and, while requiring modernisation and upgrading, presents an exciting opportunity for the purchaser to refurbish and create a home tailored to their own style and requirements.\n\nA particular feature is the size and potential of the site, with extensive garden space surrounding the dwelling. Its location combines a pleasant, established setting with excellent accessibility to town centre and its wide range of shops, schools, services and amenities.\n\nProperties offering a site of this scale within the town boundary are seldom brought to the market and the property is likely to appeal to a range of purchasers, including those seeking a substantial family home with extensive grounds, investors, or developers looking for a strategically located site with potential for future development.\n \nViewing strictly by appointment only with the agent."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch: - \nWelcoming entrance porch providing access to the main hallway and accommodation.\n\nHallway: - \nProvides access to the ground floor accommodation, with stairs leading to the first floor.\n\nLiving Room: - \nBright and spacious living room with wooden flooring, fireplace with open fire and dual-aspect windows providing excellent natural light.\n\nSitting Room: - \nSpacious sitting room with wooden flooring, fireplace with gas fire and large windows providing excellent natural light and a pleasant outlook.\n\nKitchen: - \nFitted kitchen, tiled flooring and splashback, with large windows providing plenty of natural light and a door leading to the rear garden.\n\nDining Room: - \nVersatile additional reception room, ideally suited for use as a dining room, home office or additional living space.\n\nBedroom 1: - \nGenerously proportioned double bedroom with wooden flooring and dual-aspect windows providing excellent natural light.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nBright double bedroom with wooden flooring, built-in storage and a large window.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nWell-proportioned bedroom providing versatile accommodation.\n\nBathroom: - \nBathroom comprising bath with tiled surround, WC and wash hand basin with vanity unit. Finished with wood-effect flooring.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Total floor Area: 114 sq. mts. (1227 sq ft) approx.</li><li>Site area: 0.38 HA (0.94 acres) approximately</li><li>Generous site with extensive gardens surrounding the property</li><li>Excellent potential for refurbishment and modernisation</li><li>Spacious and well-proportioned accommodation</li><li>Highly convenient location along the Old Armagh Road</li><li>Easy walking distance to town centre</li><li>Mature, established residential setting</li><li>Detached garage to the rear</li><li>Excellent potential to create a superb family home</li><li>Excellent road connectivity to Monaghan town centre and Monaghan town by-pass </li><li>Generous site offers considerable scope for further development - subject to the necessary planning permission</ul>"
      },
      {
